      "text_preview": "\n3 of 5 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:090903 Ankit Agrawal vs State Of Punjab on 12 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/89814337/\n2"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c82570be72cd40d7bb2ae8c0cbe53854_26",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "8. This Court has considered the rival submissions made by both the parties."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5f48c5a398c641a2984b890e736b38ab_27",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "9. From the perusal of the status report filed by the State, it is apparent that the proprietor of the Firm is Anil Kumar Agarwal, who is the father of the present petitioner."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5b334805fd9a4416a8e284a636fe3a89_28",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Relevant paragraph No.16 of the status report is reproduced as below:\n\"16."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cc891f557f1e4d59bbc574b5f2b26dce_29",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "That it is further submitted that information regarding license No. SKP-3/85-86 and SKP-4/85-86, issue date 25.05.1985, New license No. UP83200000241,\nUP8320000239, valid up to 31.12.2027 was sought from Drug Inspector, Firozabad and as per"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9ae6d61cf2ec4e40909ff13c3cac2159_30",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\"\n10. The veracity of the allegations levelled against the petitioner shall be established during the course of the trial."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "69a9e813d939498e971d64236e0a8c15_31",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is also apparent that the petitioner is the first time offender and he is having a valid license for running the chemist shop."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c8d5933e471c4f65a3bce119a1d4d5b0_32",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Admittedly, the petitioner is in custody since 14.12.2023 and out of a total of 18 prosecution witnesses, none has been examined till date."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2ac2e404955242d7ad96458a20b6394f_33",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "There is no other criminal case pending against him."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4707854e146941428813ae3dad523e8a_34",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Keeping in view the fact and circumstances of the case, this Court is of the view that further incarceration of the petitioner would not serve any purpose."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ebbead91cbce4d109cb5cc0e2828648c_35",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "11. As per the principle of the criminal jurisprudence, no one should be considered guilty till the guilt is proved beyond reasonable doubt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "dffca4ad0b834d1f967371c8b55c5cee_36",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Detaining the petitioner behind bars for an indefinite period would amount to violation of Article 21 of the Constitution of India and is against the principle \"Bail is a rule, jail is an exception\" as elucidated in the judgement 4 of 5 Neu"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fa33048df56f4d97914f8e2d163037fd_37",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc",
